From the , the first term of \$\left(\frac 12-x\right)^{2001}\$ is \$-x^{2001}\$, but \$x^{2001}+-x^{2001}=0\$, so the term with the largest degree is \$x^{2000}\$. So we need the coefficient of that term, as well as the coefficient of \$x^{1999}\$.
\begin{align*}\binom{2001}{1} \cdot (-x)^{2000} \cdot \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^1&=\frac{2001x^{2000}}{2}\\
